  "releaseNotes": "Serialization correctness: attribute-value whitespace (tab/newline/carriage-return) is now escaped as numeric character references (\t/\n/\n) on the result-serializer and attribute-constructor paths, which XML attribute-value normalization would otherwise collapse to spaces on re-read. Attribute escaping now routes through the shared PhoenixmlDb.Xdm.Serialization.CharacterEscaper so the XQuery and XSLT engines escape identically. Requires PhoenixmlDb.Core 1.1.9. See RELEASES.md for full notes.",
